Task: M16 - Centralize rejected HTTP response handling

Reason:
Five provider paths independently bounded and read error bodies, interpreted Retry-After, recorded diagnostics, sanitized logs, and classified equivalent HTTP failures. The copies had already diverged.

Change:
- Route Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses, Anthropic, xAI OAuth, and Codex rejected responses through one shared helper.
- Keep provider-specific behavior explicit through the existing ErrorPolicy: xAI quota handling and Codex temporary body codes/service-tier handling remain distinct.
- Keep error bodies bounded and wrapped in Zeroizing<String>; logs contain only the status and safe public error code.
- Reuse one request-route error mapper and remove the obsolete Anthropic error module and dead route display name.
- Codex HTTP 402 now follows the common payment-required classification.

